:"Mark shelf_01's local +T face. Align each end with the jig at the three listed stations measured from its front edge; drill the six pockets while the panel is still loose.","joints":[],"operation_id":"drill_shelf_01","parts":["shelf_01"],"tools":["kreg_kphj720_or_720pro","drill_driver"],"type":"drill"},{"depends_on":["set_jig"],"instruction":"Mark shelf_02's local +T face. Align each end with the jig at the three listed stations measured from its front edge; drill the six pockets while the panel is still loose.","joints":[],"operation_id":"drill_shelf_02","parts":["shelf_02"],"tools":["kreg_kphj720_or_720pro","drill_driver"],"type":"drill"},{"depends_on":["set_jig"],"instruction":"Mark top's local +T face. Align each end with the jig at the three listed stations measured from its front edge; drill the six pockets while the panel is still loose.","joints":[],"operation_id":"drill_top","parts":["top"],"tools":["kreg_kphj720_or_720pro","drill_driver"],"type":"drill"},{"depends_on":["drill_bottom","drill_shelf_01","drill_shelf_02","drill_top"],"instruction":"Dry fit the carcass on a supported work surface. Compare each labeled panel center and each clear opening to this revision's drawing; check squareness before adhesive.","joints":[],"operation_id":"dry_fit","parts":["side_left","side_right","bottom","shelf_01","shelf_02","top","back"],"tools":["square","clamps"],"type":"inspect"},{"depends_on":["dry_fit"],"instruction":"Lay side_left on a supported work surface. Apply the selected glue per its label, clamp each horizontal panel in its drawn position, and seat the three specified pocket screws at each left end without overdriving.","joints":["attach_bottom_to_side_left","attach_shelf_01_to_side_left","attach_shelf_02_to_side_left","attach_top_to_side_left"],"operation_id":"attach_left","parts":["side_left","bottom","shelf_01","shelf_02","top"],"tools":["clamps","square_drive_pocket_bit","drill_driver"],"type":"fasten"},{"depends_on":["attach_left"],"instruction":"Fit side_right to the horizontal ends, keep the carcass square, clamp the joints and seat three specified screws per right end. Keep the front open for driver access.","joints":["attach_bottom_to_side_right","attach_shelf_01_to_side_right","attach_shelf_02_to_side_right","attach_top_to_side_right"],"operation_id":"attach_right","parts":["side_right","bottom","shelf_01","shelf_02","top"],"tools":["clamps","square_drive_pocket_bit","drill_driver"],"type":"fasten"},{"depends_on":["attach_right"],"instruction":"Support the square carcass face-down. Transfer the listed carcass-edge centerlines to back, apply wood glue per its label, clamp the back flush, and drive only the specified 1-1/4 in brads on those lines. Check the thin back and all edges for unintended breakout.","joints":["attach_side_left_to_back","attach_side_right_to_back","attach_bottom_to_back","attach_shelf_01_to_back","attach_shelf_02_to_back","attach_top_to_back"],"operation_id":"attach_back","parts":["side_left","side_right","bottom","shelf_01","shelf_02","top","back"],"tools":["clamps","18g_brad_nailer_1_25in_compatible","square"],"type":"fasten"},{"depends_on":["attach_back"],"instruction":"Allow adhesive to cure per its label. Check squareness, finished dimensions, clear openings, seated fasteners and breakout. Before use, arrange site-specific tip-over restraint and record the physical review; no shelf load rating is supplied.","joints":[],"operation_id":"final_check","parts":["side_left","side_right","bottom","shelf_01","shelf_02","top","back"],"tools":["square","measuring_tools"],"type":"inspect"}],"physical_review":"not_reviewed","recipe_id":"kreg720_19_05_14in_bookcase","recipe_version":"1.0.0","required_tools":["kreg_kphj720_or_720pro","supplied_easy_set_bit_and_collar","square_drive_pocket_bit","drill_driver","clamps","panel_saw","square","measuring_tools","18g_brad_nailer_1_25in_compatible"],"resolved_sha256":"9eaedec6809341739d3e8bd1e525a3133250495cc8ba5947cf26fc3526cc0fef","review_record":{"load_rating":null,"physical_record":null,"technical_scope":"Source, dimensions, local stations, named joint coverage and software dependency checks"},"revision_id":"rev_a5ce69cef4f84c18bc2726bad98a575d","source_records":[{"rule":"Gauge actual stock, select the 3/4 range stop collar and 1-1/4 in screw; clamp joints. Panel guide stations: 5/8 to 1-1/2 in from edges and 6 to 8 in apart.","source_id":"kreg720_manual","title":"KPHJ720/720PRO Global manual, 06/2020 104909 V1, English pages 12-17","url":"https://www.kregtool.com/on/demandware.static/-/Library-Sites-RefArchSharedLibrary/default/dw59d64a56/manuals/KPHJ720PRO_Global.pdf"},{"rule":"Actual thickness governs selection. Coarse thread is preferred for plywood; zinc pocket screws are for indoor dry use.","source_id":"kreg_screw_guide","title":"Kreg screw guide, updated June 29, 2026","url":"https://learn.kregtool.com/learn/how-to-select-right-pocket-hole-screw/"},{"rule":"Published method uses 1-1/4 in pocket screws and wood glue, with a separately attached 1/4 in plywood back, wood glue and 1-1/4 in brads. Original dimensions and quantities are not reused.","source_id":"kreg_bookcase","title":"Kreg / The Creative Mom Built In Bookcase","url":"https://learn.kregtool.com/plans/built-in-bookcase/"},{"rule":"The indoor steel 18-gauge pack includes 1-1/4 in brads. Select that length; do not mix the other pack lengths into this recipe.","source_id":"dewalt_brad","title":"DEWALT DWBN18PP 18-gauge brad project pack","url":"https://www.dewalt.com/en-us/product/dwbn18pp/18-gauge-brad-nail-project-pack"}],"spec_sha256":"e44d9f09f593efb98fe8cc4da6505196e45b01f9e4012e8ba5e391ae3b35d409","status":"complete","technical_completeness":true,"validation_findings":[]}